        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Companies: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia\n- Topics: NASCAR Cup Series title sponsorship, essay contests\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo purchased Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky.\n- From 2007 to 2011, former title sponsor Crown Royal named the Toyota Owners 400 after the winner of an essay contest held during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway NASCAR Cup Series races each year, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring as the first race.",
